//? Title: HRNet persistent resolution and repeated exchange
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Accurate pixel labels need broad context while retaining spatial detail. HRNet keeps several resolutions active and repeatedly exchanges their features. This report checks odd-grid route values and derivatives,then visibly fits the complete compact tensor model and inspects its held-out masks and streams.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/hrnet.cpp`.

> The method

Persistent high-to-low streams exchange by projected bilinear upsampling or learned stride2 chains. Repeated sum/ReLU fusion supplies every target with every source. Final aligned concatenation predicts image-sized logits;explicit Adam optimizes all routes with paired BN checkpoints.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/hrnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/hrnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/hrnet_concept.tikz > build/hrnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/hrnet_concept.svg build/hrnet_concept.dvi > build/hrnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
